cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use gemQC-pilot, please cite it as below, together with libint, the
  Basis Set Exchange and the papers of the methods used (see README.md, References).
title: "gemQC-pilot: quantum chemistry with geminals"
abstract: >-
  gemQC-pilot implements SCF, MP2, MP2-F12 and a pilot version of MP2-F12XG
  (geminals bound to groups of basis functions), with a C++ backend (integrals
  with libint) and a Python frontend.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andreas
    family-names: Köhn
    affiliation: University of Stuttgart
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/KoehnLab/gemQC-pilot"
keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - explicitly correlated methods
  - F12
  - geminals
  - MP2-F12
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Libint: a library for the evaluation of molecular integrals of many-body operators over Gaussian functions"
    authors:
      - given-names: Edward F.
        family-names: Valeev
    version: 2.13.1
    url: "http://libint.valeyev.net"
  - type: article
    title: "A New Basis Set Exchange: An Open, Up-to-Date Resource for the Molecular Sciences Community"
    authors:
      - given-names: Benjamin P.
        family-names: Pritchard
      - given-names: Doaa
        family-names: Altarawy
      - given-names: Brett
        family-names: Didier
      - given-names: Tara D.
        family-names: Gibson
      - given-names: Theresa L.
        family-names: Windus
    journal: "Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling"
    volume: 59
    start: 4814
    year: 2019
    doi: "10.1021/acs.jcim.9b00725"
